# Documentation Workflow

## After Every Task Completion

| Document | Update trigger |
| -------- | -------------- |
| `implementation-plan.md` | Mark task checkbox; update Sprint Progress Tracker |
| `acceptance-criteria.md` | Mark criterion status Completed when verified |
| `README.md` | Update only if setup, run, or test steps change |
| `tool-workflow.md` | Update "Pending" sections as implementation phases complete |
| `ai-prompts/` | At sprint Quality Gate — update relevant activity file (see `ai-prompts/README.md`) |

## Hard Rules

- Do **not** silently edit `requirements-analysis.md` — it is the approved business authority
- Do **not** mark acceptance criteria Completed without verification
- Do **not** leave `implementation-plan.md` sprint checkboxes unchecked after approved work
- Do **not** update `tool-workflow.md` with work that has not actually been done

## Acceptance Criteria Status Values

`Not Started` → `In Progress` → `Completed`

Only advance status after manual test, integration test, or code review confirms the criterion.

## Prompt History Discipline

- At sprint Quality Gate: update the relevant file in `ai-prompts/` (e.g. `testing.md` after QA sprint)
- Use continuation template (Template I) in `docs/reusable-workflow.md` for scope-frozen prompts
- Log verbatim prompts when available — note honestly when transcript is unavailable
- Honest logging only — never fabricate sessions or mark prompts as iterated when they were not
